      },
      "title": "You press Enter",
      "description": "**What it is:** the key handler for the chat box.\n\n**How it works:** every key press runs this. Enter (without Shift) blocks the browser's default action and submits. Shift+Enter makes a new line. Typing `@` saves the cursor position and opens the command palette for picking accounts.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is the first line of code your message touches.\n\n**Watch out:** `e.preventDefault()` matters. Without it, Enter would also add a line break to the box."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-input.tsx",
      "line": 308,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 298,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 308,
          "character": 4
        }
      },
      "title": "handleSubmit",
      "description": "**What it is:** the submit function.\n\n**How it works:** read the text and trim the spaces. Stop if it's empty or a reply is still running. Otherwise call `onSend(text)`, the function the container passed in (tour 03), then clear the box.\n\n**Why it matters:** the input's job ends here. From now on, the container is in charge.\n\n**Watch out:** the box is cleared **straight away**, before the message is sent. If sending fails, your text is no longer in the box, though it still shows in the chat."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
      "line": 192,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 191,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 192,
          "character": 62
        }
      },
      "title": "The container takes over",
      "description": "**What it is:** `handleSendMessage`, the function that runs the whole send. The next steps go through it in order.\n\n**How it works:** a guard comes first. Do nothing if the text is blank, a reply is already loading, or you have no connected accounts.\n\n**Why it matters:** one message at a time keeps the chat history in order.\n\n**Watch out:** the guard returns silently. The input is already disabled in those cases, so users rarely hit it."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
      "line": 234,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 194,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 234,
          "character": 6
        }
      },
      "title": "Cancelling old approvals",
      "description": "**What it is:** clean-up before sending.\n\n**How it works:** if an earlier reply is still waiting for you to Allow or Deny a tool, sending a new message cancels it. The code adds a `tool_cancelled` event to that old message and marks the approval as `false`.\n\n**Why it matters:** an old approval no longer makes sense once you've moved on. Approving it later could change your ad account by surprise.\n\n**Watch out:** in `pendingApprovals`, `null` means *still waiting*, `true` means approved, and `false` means denied or cancelled."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
      "line": 238,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 236,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 238,
          "character": 55
        }
      },
      "title": "Token and cancel switch",
      "description": "**How it works:** get your login token. Then cancel any request that's still running (`abort()`) and create a new `AbortController` for this one.\n\n**New idea — AbortController:** a cancel switch for `fetch`. The request gets its `signal`, and calling `abort()` stops it.\n\n**Why it matters:** the Stop button and leaving the page both use it to cut off a running answer.\n\n**Watch out:** the old request is cancelled *before* the new one starts, so two answers never stream into the same chat."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/components/chat/chat-container.tsx",
      "line": 248,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 240,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 248,
          "character": 6
        }
      },
      "title": "Creating the chat",
      "description": "**What it is:** the first message of a new chat creates a chat record in the database.\n\n**How it works:** `createSession` sends the first 2,000 characters as the title. Then `window.history.replaceState` changes the address to `/chat/<id>` without reloading the page.\n\n**Why it matters:** the chat now has a permanent address, so reloading brings it back.\n\n**Watch out:** if creating the chat fails, `sessionId` stays `null` and the chat still works. It just isn't saved."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/src/hooks/chat/useChatSession.ts",
      "line": 31,
      "selection": {
